<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Steers plans capitalisation issue.</title>
<headline>Steers plans capitalisation issue.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fast-food retailer Steers Holdings Ltd announced on Monday it planned to create a new class of &quot;N&quot; shares to improve its capital structure.</p>
<p>It said 26.366 million &quot;N&quot; shares would be issued in the ratio of one for every ordinary share held.</p>
<p>The capitalisation issue would double the number of shares in issue, resulting in its share price, earnings per share and net asset value being halved.</p>
<p>The last day to register for the issue would be January 24 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
